{"entries":[{"canonical_text":"The MESSAGE, AGGREGATE, and UPDATE functions of any message-passing GNN are replaced by their quaternion counterparts so that the layerwise message-passing semantics are preserved in quaternion space.","content_hash":"edeb19a92e26fad410c02f98e5afea02851abf61b5bd569e480266f356521441","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":[],"knowledge_id":"claim_1","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":[],"search_text":"claim_1 The MESSAGE, AGGREGATE, and UPDATE functions of any message-passing GNN are replaced by their quaternion counterparts so that the layerwise message-passing semantics are preserved in quaternion space.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_1","anchor_paragraph_p0033"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"Representing layer weights as quaternion matrices and grouping four real feature channels into one quaternion reduces the number of independent trainable real parameters by a factor of four relative to an equivalent real-valued GNN weight matrix.","content_hash":"8ed8cd7732c0cdfd78eb7551918d2df8f7994e40d864da84a40cabebb5fbd606","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":[],"knowledge_id":"claim_2","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":["lcs_d34f2f4a3eedc56d"],"search_text":"claim_2 Representing layer weights as quaternion matrices and grouping four real feature channels into one quaternion reduces the number of independent trainable real parameters by a factor of four relative to an equivalent real-valued GNN weight matrix.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_2","anchor_paragraph_p0042"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"A quaternion weight mapping from $F$ real input features to $F'$ real outputs uses $F/4\\times F'/4$ quaternion entries, yielding one-fourth the degrees of freedom of the corresponding real weight matrix.","content_hash":"ee0ac1ac6d224fdc5b961db288976e0a317c99528ee70ae5bc9ff00d4f32d2e1","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":[],"knowledge_id":"claim_3","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":[],"search_text":"claim_3 A quaternion weight mapping from $F$ real input features to $F'$ real outputs uses $F/4\\times F'/4$ quaternion entries, yielding one-fourth the degrees of freedom of the corresponding real weight matrix.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_3","anchor_paragraph_p0042"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"Quaternion matrix multiplications have the same asymptotic time complexity as the corresponding real matrix multiplications.","content_hash":"91e0fa54220616f11eb1ec3722f2565c3bcc89db45412a9b874c69166e1e6a59","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":[],"knowledge_id":"claim_4","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":["lcs_d34f2f4a3eedc56d"],"search_text":"claim_4 Quaternion matrix multiplications have the same asymptotic time complexity as the corresponding real matrix multiplications.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_4","anchor_paragraph_p0042"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"The parameter reduction described in claim 2 is achieved without increasing matrix-multiplication time complexity. [Referenced claim 2: Representing layer weights as quaternion matrices and grouping four real feature channels into one quaternion reduces the number of independent trainable real parameters by a factor of four relative to an equivalent real-valued GNN weight matrix.]","content_hash":"7322690ad0e0e64aa8f0c447aa08e6ab787ac0b507fdeae796ff343ad0589cee","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":["lcs_d34f2f4a3eedc56d"],"knowledge_id":"claim_5","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":[],"search_text":"claim_5 The parameter reduction described in claim 2 is achieved without increasing matrix-multiplication time complexity. [Referenced claim 2: Representing layer weights as quaternion matrices and grouping four real feature channels into one quaternion reduces the number of independent trainable real parameters by a factor of four relative to an equivalent real-valued GNN weight matrix.]","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_5","anchor_claim_2","anchor_paragraph_p0042"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"When QMPNN variants of standard GNN architectures are trained under the same hyperparameters as those standard GNN architectures and evaluated on standard datasets, the quaternion models achieve comparable or better accuracy, ROC-AUC, or Hits@K (proportion of top-K predictions that are correct) while using roughly one-fourth of the trainable parameters of those standard GNN architectures.","content_hash":"8b0f230351080f754f1121df4509871d59f22fbb5f4678a5a42d8554a98f45d6","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":["lcs_135bb429535ad08e"],"knowledge_id":"claim_6","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":[],"search_text":"claim_6 When QMPNN variants of standard GNN architectures are trained under the same hyperparameters as those standard GNN architectures and evaluated on standard datasets, the quaternion models achieve comparable or better accuracy, ROC-AUC, or Hits@K (proportion of top-K predictions that are correct) while using roughly one-fourth of the trainable parameters of those standard GNN architectures.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_6","anchor_paragraph_p0071"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"(a) node classification on Cora: real GCN 85.2 ± 1.3 accuracy with 140.5K parameters vs QGCN 84.1 ± 1.5 accuracy with 42.1K parameters;","content_hash":"9843071eea487f89f37dcae005431c09c67d7f2aef4186e8f1dbbd7cf3e9ce15","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":[],"kno