c75c2b0bf6e14a0d9a","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":[],"knowledge_id":"claim_10","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":["operator_equivalence_Eclaim_10_Oclaim_10"],"search_text":"claim_10 (d) graph classification on MUTAG: GCN 83.54 ± 0.40 accuracy with 4.8K parameters vs QGCN 88.61 ± 0.66 accuracy with 4.4K parameters.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_10","anchor_paragraph_p0069"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"Across all tasks and datasets evaluated, quaternion variants of standard GNN architectures frequently perform within a small margin of the corresponding real models and sometimes exceed their performance while consistently having approximately one-fourth the trainable parameter count of the corresponding real models.","content_hash":"346cdbb7b6fc39f740e978566cf9fc1d7b07eb24e4c212ef68dc9f8a7fd57e97","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":[],"knowledge_id":"claim_11","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":[],"search_text":"claim_11 Across all tasks and datasets evaluated, quaternion variants of standard GNN architectures frequently perform within a small margin of the corresponding real models and sometimes exceed their performance while consistently having approximately one-fourth the trainable parameter count of the corresponding real models.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_11","anchor_paragraph_p0064"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"Winning graph-lottery tickets exist for both real-valued GNNs and QMPNNs.","content_hash":"57028db844d04b3aebda58ffa23b9361ce070430d83e64ce169d0fec40240705","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":["lcs_3da0caa1875756c3"],"knowledge_id":"claim_12","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":[],"search_text":"claim_12 Winning graph-lottery tickets exist for both real-valued GNNs and QMPNNs.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_12","anchor_paragraph_p0017"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"Magnitude-based iterative pruning identifies subnetworks that match baseline performance at sparsity levels down to approximately 1–20% of the original parameter count across multiple architectures and tasks.","content_hash":"df18b9aed17946398f40a6427ce5c7b9bfb1c2b68d364865bb864ce73db9cf7d","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":["lcs_a5034605309ee286"],"knowledge_id":"claim_13","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":["lcs_3da0caa1875756c3"],"search_text":"claim_13 Magnitude-based iterative pruning identifies subnetworks that match baseline performance at sparsity levels down to approximately 1–20% of the original parameter count across multiple architectures and tasks.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_13","anchor_paragraph_p0072"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"QMPNN variants scale to large graph datasets and maintain performance comparable to real-valued GNNs while using fewer parameters.","content_hash":"ccc5685b4f20ec4cffb20308b1bb58912f993fa7c789922eb9066faa76d7b8c7","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":["lcs_0f2fafb498fd2ade","lcs_a5e9bfef2f3a9073"],"knowledge_id":"claim_14","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":["operator_relation_2_ast_1"],"search_text":"claim_14 QMPNN variants scale to large graph datasets and maintain performance comparable to real-valued GNNs while using fewer parameters.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_14","anchor_paragraph_p0073"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"on OGBN-Arxiv node classification, GCN achieves 72.8 ± 1.5 accuracy with 145.1K parameters versus QGCN 72.3 ± 1.6 with 43.5K parameters;","content_hash":"c9b198e36d64f802bb9568c1f9962cfeafb00a9f821298981698c48cec428178","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":[],"knowledge_id":"claim_15","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":["operator_equivalence_Eclaim_15_Oclaim_15","operator_relation_2_ast_1"],"search_text":"claim_15 on OGBN-Arxiv node classification, GCN achieves 72.8 ± 1.5 accuracy with 145.1K parameters versus QGCN 72.3 ± 1.6 with 43.5K parameters;","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_15","anchor_paragraph_p0062"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"on OGBG-COLLAB link prediction, QGCN achieves Hits@50 45.80 ± 1.35 with 6.4K parameters compared to GCN 44.02 ± 1.57 with 12.5K parameters.","content_hash":"fb37fcc9435885fb2e19534fe8a62ad2e2238d45941cd6749c47f1df9a13f6d5","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":[],"knowledge_id":"claim_16","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":["operator_equivalence_Eclaim_16_Oclaim_16","operator_relation_2_ast_2"],"search_text":"claim_16 on OGBG-COLLAB link prediction, QGCN achieves Hits@50 45.80 ± 1.35 with 6.4K parameters compared to GCN 44.02 ± 1.57 with 12.5K parameters.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_16","anchor_paragraph_p0065"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"the quaternion reparameterization is effective on large-scale graph benchmarks.","content_hash":"3968ca1b1e6ec26d560c24623c669e19d49c860ab3358e414072ef2a913c9af9","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":1,"incoming_reasoning":["lcs_c3c824e0a480ac10"],"knowledge_id":"claim_17","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":[],"search_text":"claim_17 the quaternion reparameterization is effective on large-scale graph benchmarks.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_17","anchor_paragraph_p0032"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"When the three QMPNN variants QGCN, QGAT, and QSAGE of standard GNN architectures are trained under the same hy