parameters, whereas QGCN attains a ROC-AUC of 83.55 ± 0.03 with 27.2K parameters.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_claim_9","anchor_paragraph_p0065"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"In the case of a weight-pruned fraction of 0.3, GLT models pointed out by red and green stars give results on node classification (OGBN-ARXIV), link prediction (OGBL-COLLAB), and graph classification (OGBG-MOHLIV) that are comparable with those of the pre-pruning baselines indicated by dashed lines, that is, they are comparable even under sparsity.","content_hash":"05415e6a2f9a1c10f8024a5478620a14289f26ef9bf74baf3787dda00e954b5f","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":2,"incoming_reasoning":[],"knowledge_id":"claim_E07","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":["operator_equivalence_E07_O07"],"search_text":"claim_E07 In the case of a weight-pruned fraction of 0.3, GLT models pointed out by red and green stars give results on node classification (OGBN-ARXIV), link prediction (OGBL-COLLAB), and graph classification (OGBG-MOHLIV) that are comparable with those of the pre-pruning baselines indicated by dashed lines, that is, they are comparable even under sparsity.","source_anchor_ids":["anchor_paragraph_p0058"],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"public"},{"canonical_text":"conjunction(claim_14,claim_15)","content_hash":"941d756773396e0d104a925c7650332ff31b0450a2e4f13fe96ae6912c9daf91","current_step":5,"external_ids":[],"first_seen_step":3,"incoming_reasoning":["operator_relation_2_ast_1"],"knowledge_id":"helper_relation_2_1","languages":[],"non_reasoning_links":[],"outgoing_reasoning":["operator_relation_2_ast_2"],"search_text":"helper_relation_2_1 conjunction(claim_14,claim_15)","source_anchor_ids":[],"title":null,"type":"claim","visibility":"formal_internal"},{"canonical_text":"conjunction(helper_relation_2_1,claim_16)","content_hash":"f64feaf8543ec7de6e8475d310de2fc5ede5e8816c879d3ecbf39d1bafbdb5ca","current_step